# Core Guardrails

- Prefer root-cause fixes over symptom-hiding workarounds.
- Keep diffs focused and minimal for the requested scope.
- Do not use destructive git commands unless explicitly requested.
- Do not commit secrets, local machine paths, or local-only config files.
- Add or update tests for behavior changes.
- Run lint, typecheck, and relevant tests before claiming completion.
- Keep comments concise and durable; avoid storyline/ticket-history comments in source.
